# Word formation lab

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `wordformation-v2.json` | **The only file you edit.** All words, sentences, rules and affix notes. |
| `template.html` | The page code. Change it only for new features. |
| `build.py` | Checks the JSON and builds the two pages below. |
| `index.html` | Fetches the JSON when it loads. Must be served (see below). |
| `wordformation-standalone.html` | Has the JSON inside it. Works by double-click or e-mail. |

## Everyday workflow
1. Edit `wordformation-v2.json`.
2. Run `python build.py` (it lists any mistakes in the data).
3. Standalone: send the file. Hosted: upload `index.html` once, then only replace the JSON when the words change. Learners just refresh.

## Running `index.html` locally
Browsers block `file://` pages from reading other files. In this folder run:

    python -m http.server

then open http://localhost:8000. On a school site or any web host, upload `index.html` and the JSON to the same folder.

You can point the page at a different bank with `index.html?data=other-bank.json`.

## Learner progress
Saved in the browser (per device). It is keyed by `base:word`, so it survives edits unless you rename a word.
